If this is indeed the older DS20 model and not the DS20E, we experienced
two hardware related incidences with them over the last few years.

1) Crashes with kernel trap illegal memory write accesses.
   These were caused by CPUs with too low a revision for 5.1a, according
   to an internal FCO. The CPUs were replaced.

2) Hangs with no response from console.  This turned out to be a bad
   front panel display that was replaced, also an internally known problem.

Perhaps, if you have the proper HP support, you could ask them if
either of these known DS20 hardware issues might be the cause. Things
reported as CPU errors can sometimes difficult to ascertain.
