This does NOT apply to the boot volume.  AdvFS only allows 1 volume in 
the boot (root) volume.  However, /usr, /var, and another other file 
system/domains can use the addvol/rmvol trick.

The reason the boot root domain can not have more than one disk, is that 
the boot firmware does not know how to deal with multiple disks in order 
to find all the parts of vmunix.  And it can be a chicken and an egg 
situation since /etc/advfs/... is where the list of disks are stored, 
and if the for some reason /etc/advfs is _NOT_ on the disk specified to 
be booted, there is no way to find the other disks.

                                        Bob Harris


