In article <pan.2004.08.19.21.24.26.963209@aero-graphics.com>,
 jason <jnielsen@aero-graphics.com> wrote:

> Are there any known issues with advfs domains greater than ~1.2TB on
> Tru64 4.0f?

Domains, No.  Partitions, yes.

> We have a 1.5TB advfs domain. Under showfdmns it shows up fine. df on the
> other hand does not show the domain correctly.
> 
> ema_domain#ema_raid              -618892672   652597693   875729448    43%    
> /aja
> 
> Im having samba and nfs clients having issues with this as well. Even some
> nfsv3 clients are reporting incorrect details. I suspect the nfs clients
> in the later cases and the samba server on tru64 as the culprit smb side.

That is to say, an AdvFS domain can be as big as 256TB if you max it out 
with 256 1TB volumes.

_BUT_ each volume _MUST_ be 1TB-1 or less.  If you have any volumes 
greater than 1TB, you may be experiencing data corruption.

As for df, it is very likely to be using some 32 bit values and getting 
overflow when doing addition and multiplications.  Similar problems may 
be experienced with the statfs(), statvfs(), and stat() system calls.  
Many of these 32 bit issues were clean up in Tru64 UNIX v5.*

                                        Bob Harris


